   "source": [
    "🐍 Python Data Structures: Theory + Practical Use *\n",
    "1. List (list)\n",
    "\n",
    "- Ordered collection\n",
    "- Mutable (can change)\n",
    "- Allows duplicates\n",
    "- Access using index\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "236ad410-ffda-4dd0-a273-f427f499cbc6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "🌍 Real-World Practical Example"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "4d627875-f813-48ac-8468-a0266d00acb9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "['apple', 'milk', 'bread']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "cart = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"milk\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add item\n",
    "cart.append(\"bread\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Remove item\n",
    "cart.remove(\"banana\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(cart)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "77b4c28d-2738-48b0-9af7-76cd3287ff9d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "💡 Why List here?\n",
    "Items change frequently (add/remove)\n",
    "Order matters (user sees items in sequence)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "ee90cc39-fd93-43ac-a579-2215c22bcb01",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "🔹 2. Tuple (tuple)\n",
    "\n",
    "* Ordered collection\n",
    "* Immutable (cannot change)\n",
    "* Faster than list\n",
    "* Fixed structure\n",
    "🌍 Real-World Practical Example\n",
    "📍 GPS Location System"
   ]
  },
